# Line endings are LF everywhere — in the repository and in every working tree.
# `eol=lf` pins checkout to LF regardless of platform (core.eol defaults to
# "native", i.e. CRLF on Windows, which is why `text=auto` alone is not enough
# here). Git still auto-detects binary files and leaves them untouched. Matches
# .editorconfig (end_of_line = lf).
#
# History: added 2026-09-04 after a file move flipped CRLF->LF on CRLF files and
# broke git's rename detection. With no policy the tree had drifted into a
# CRLF/LF mix; this makes git normalize on commit so no tool can reintroduce it.
* text=auto eol=lf
